      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m reading this correctly, if isKeepingUp is false, then the code can never reach l.3591, which means we could just return false immediately. This also gives an opportunity to clarify the comment above I think, something like :\n\n  // If a request is not multilayer, and it\u0027s a LISTEN or TRACK_DEFAULT, then it won\u0027t\n  // keep up a network satisfying it.\n  if (!multilayer \u0026\u0026 !isRequest) return false;",
